        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Gadolinium and nickel nitrates, H3dmpa, sodium sulfate, and thiodiglycolic acid were dissolved in water and methanol. After stirring for 48 h, freshly prepared aqueous NaOH (3.0 M) was added dropwise until incipient permanent precipitation. The mixture was filtered, sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined stainless-steel vessel, and heated at 140 °C for 2 days. It was cooled to room temperature at approximately 2 °C/h. Green block-shaped crystals were collected by filtration, washed with water, and dried in air. H3dmpa served to adjust pH and is not incorporated as a coordinating ligand.",
